Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.10,Header,,0,0,0,,This is a Gentlemen of the Hàn free fansub.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.86,0:00:06.54,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,1100,4900,5660)\pos(653.755,490.255)}Episode 58\N\N\N\N\NThe Drowning \Nof the Seven Armies
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.20,0:00:14.76,Thinking,,0,0,0,,In the fall of the 24th year\N of the Jian'an era, 219 CE,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.76,0:00:19.70,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei, at the exhortation of \NZhuge Liang and other officials,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.70,0:00:22.04,Thinking,,0,0,0,,and despite refusing many times,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.04,0:00:25.24,Thinking,,0,0,0,,mounted the altar at Mianyang to receive obeisance
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.24,0:00:28.81,Thinking,,0,0,0,,and named himself the King of Hanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.22,0:00:36.62,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,2060,2380)\pos(966.667,442.667)}Liú Bèi\NStyled: Xuándé
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.81,0:00:32.48,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He made his son\N Liu Shan Crown Prince,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.48,0:00:37.54,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang as Strategist-General to manage military and state matters,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.54,0:00:41.78,Thinking,,0,0,0,,and named Guan Yu, Zhang Fei, Zhao Yun,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.78,0:00:46.65,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Ma Chao, and Huang Zhong \Nas the Five Tiger Generals.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.06,0:00:50.30,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,2900,3220)\pos(314.755,433.455)}Cáo Cāo\NStyled: Mèngdé
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.16,0:00:52.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Liu Bei is just a mat-weaving knave!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.96,0:00:55.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}How dare he call himself\N the King of Hanzhong?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.43,0:00:59.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Insolent bastard, I swear to extinguish him!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.93,0:01:04.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Pass my orders! \NMuster all the troops of the state today!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.19,0:01:06.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}I shall subjugate \Nthe Riverlands once more!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.96,0:01:10.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Only by destroying \Nthis traitor can I be content!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.04,0:01:17.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Your Highness, do not let a brief moment of fury drive you into another far expedition.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.76,0:01:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}I have a plan that, without drawing a bow and nocking an arrow,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.00,0:01:24.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}can make Liu Bei fall prey to disaster!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.12,0:01:25.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Once his army becomes feeble,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.79,0:01:28.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}only one general will be \Nneeded to subdue him!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.34,0:01:30.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Victory would then come!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.72,0:01:32.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Zhongda, what worthy view do you have?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.70,0:01:35.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}In the past, Sun Quan\N married his sister to Liu Bei,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.70,0:01:37.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}then later lured her back to his domain.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.94,0:01:40.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}But Liu Bei also never\N returned Jing Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.39,0:01:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Thus they harbor \Nmutual teeth-grinding hatred.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.07,0:01:47.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Sire, send most eloquent of emissaries to give a letter to Sun Quan about the matter,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.50,0:01:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}persuading him to \Nmuster troops to attack Jing Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.63,0:01:53.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Liu Bei would send the troops of the Riverlands over there,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.68,0:01:56.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}then your Majesty\N may exploit the distraction
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.50,0:01:58.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}and advance an army to take Hanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.38,0:02:03.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Is this not twice the result with half the effort, winning all in a single stroke?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.79,0:02:06.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}A worthy view indeed, Zhongda!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.22,0:02:15.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}I suppose Man Boning \Ncan be the emissary
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.44,0:02:17.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}to be sent to Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.18,0:02:25.14,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,2545,2940)\pos(941.333,442.667)}Sūn Quán\NStyled: Zhòngmóu
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.05,0:02:28.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Marquis of Wu, \NWu and Wei have no conflict,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.48,0:02:33.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}and only the tension between us \Nhas been instigated by Liu Bei.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.42,0:02:36.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}The King of Wei sent me here
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.13,0:02:39.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}to arrange an attack on\N Jing Province with you, General.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.08,0:02:41.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}He will march on\N Hanzhong and the Riverlands
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.78,0:02:43.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}in order to make a pincer attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.34,0:02:46.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}After Liu Bei is defeated,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.14,0:02:50.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}we will divide his land and \Nswear not to invade each other!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.79,0:02:58.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Let Man Boning have a rest \Nin the manor. Do not neglect him.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.19,0:03:01.32,Default,,0,0,0,,That is appreciated, your Lordship.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.83,0:03:09.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Gentlemen, would you like to speak?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.24,0:03:12.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Wei and Wu never had any rivalry,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.11,0:03:14.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}it is only due to \NZhuge Liang's persuasion
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.72,0:03:18.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}that the two have been fighting each other for years without stopping.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.54,0:03:21.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}This has brought\N disaster to the common folk.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.78,0:03:26.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Man Chong's arrival today shows\N that Cao Cao wishes for peace with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.57,0:03:30.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}I believe we should\N invade and seize Jing Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.65,0:03:31.74,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,My lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.31,0:03:38.34,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Although Man Chong was here \Nto influence us, there is reason in his words.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.74,0:03:35.94,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,1820,2180)\pos(960.8,436.8)}Gù Yōng\NStyled: Yuántàn
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.80,0:03:43.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, you may, on one hand,\N send Man Chong to inform Cao Cao,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.97,0:03:49.40,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,then, on the other hand, send people \Nover the Yangzi river to spy on Guan Yu.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.66,0:03:52.19,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Thereon, act according to the situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.33,0:03:54.40,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.31,0:03:59.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, I received news that Cao Cao named Man Chong as Chief of Staff
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.91,0:04:03.14,Default,,0,0,0,,and sent him to Fancheng to discuss raising an army with Cao Ren.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.14,0:04:05.76,Default,,0,0,0,,He also colluded with\N Sun Quan to gain naval support.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.76,0:04:06.79,Default,,0,0,0,,They will take Jing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.79,0:04:09.05,Default,,0,0,0,,How should this be handled?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.89,0:04:14.08,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, I expected that Cao Cao would have such a plot.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.08,0:04:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,However, Wu has many strategists and Sun Quan is cautious,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.79,0:04:20.80,Default,,0,0,0,,he wants Cao Cao to order \NCao Ren to raise the army first.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.80,0:04:23.16,Default,,0,0,0,,What should we do in that case?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.16,0:04:29.36,Default,,0,0,0,,An emissary should be sent to Yunchang with orders to attack Fancheng first.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.36,0:04:32.88,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,This way, the enemy will be \Nfrightened and collapse by itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.86,0:04:34.58,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,3450,3700)\pos(344,453.333)}Zhūgě Liàng\NStyled: Kǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.88,0:04:34.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Great!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.02,0:04:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,The Major of the Front, Fei Shi will be sent as the emissary to Jing now.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.85,0:04:51.47,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Your Highness, Guan Yu has taken Xiangyang
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.47,0:04:53.33,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,and has besieged Fancheng heavily.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.60,0:04:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is Cao Ren?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.31,0:04:58.81,Default,,0,0,0,,He is being assaulted\N by Guan Yu at Fancheng.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.81,0:05:01.94,Default,,0,0,0,,He begs your Majesty to send\N a general with troops for aid.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.30,0:05:04.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Wenze!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.09,0:05:06.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I am here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.33,0:05:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you willing to\N break the siege at Fancheng?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.05,0:05:10.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.36,0:05:16.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, please appoint a\N general as the vanguard to go with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.74,0:05:20.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is willing to be the vanguard?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.40,0:05:25.43,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, I will \Ndo so with utmost loyalty.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.43,0:05:28.10,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I shall capture Guan Yu \Nand present him to you!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.38,0:05:30.10,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,1380,1700)\pos(973.333,468)}Yú Jìn\NStyled: Wénzé
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.57,0:05:34.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I normally do not harbor suspicions,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.05,0:05:40.97,Default,,0,0,0,,but Ma Chao, your old master,\N and Pang Rou, your elder brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.97,0:05:44.09,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,both serve Liu Bei\N in the Western Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.19,0:05:47.88,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Even if I do not doubt you,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.88,0:05:50.90,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,there are other voices\N that will not be silent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.65,0:05:54.15,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Ever since I submitted \Nto you at Hanzhong,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.15,0:05:57.94,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I am grateful for your great generosity that I cannot repay even with my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.94,0:06:01.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Ma Chao, my old master, \Nwas brave but had no strategy,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.22,0:06:00.78,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,2250,2540)\pos(341.333,501.333)}Páng Dé\NStyled: Lìngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.02,0:06:04.44,Default,,0,0,0,,causing the loss of his land and\N him entering the Riverlands alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.02,0:06:08.98,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Today, we serve our own masters.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.98,0:06:11.22,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Our old bonds are severed!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.18,0:06:16.57,Default,,0,0,0,,How could I dare harbor treachery with all the kindness you have given me?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.57,0:06:18.58,Default,,0,0,0,,May your Highness see this clearly!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.64,0:06:50.68,Default,,0,0,0,,With General Pang's great loyalty, \Nhow can we not risk our lives with him?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.97,0:06:53.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}If I am killed by Guan Yu,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.57,0:06:58.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}you will put my corpse into this coffin.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.42,0:07:01.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}If I kill Guan Yu,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.63,0:07:04.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}take his head and put it into this coffin.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.04,0:07:05.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}It will be a gift to his Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.01,0:07:10.26,Default,,0,0,0,,We swear to follow General Pang to fight Guan Yu to the death!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.17,0:07:12.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Carry the coffin and march out!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.95,0:07:25.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Report!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.63,0:07:32.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Orders from the King, Guan Yu is both wise and brave, be vigilant.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.34,0:07:35.43,Default,,0,0,0,,If you can attack, attack, \Nbut if not, then defend carefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.43,0:07:38.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Why does his Highness\N see Guan Yu as important?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.13,0:07:41.90,Default,,0,0,0,,When I advance against him,\N I will puncture his reputation!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.25,0:07:46.17,Default,,0,0,0,,The words of the King must be obeyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.78,0:07:49.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Men, beat the drums and march!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.54,0:07:52.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us quickly advance to \NFancheng and fight Guan Yu!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.22,0:07:58.10,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,General, Cao Cao has sent Yu Jin \Nwith seven columns of elite soldiers
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.10,0:07:59.42,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,to reinforce Fancheng.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.42,0:08:01.50,Default,,0,0,0,,A coffin is hoisted at their front,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.50,0:08:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,challenging you to a fight to the death.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.60,0:08:09.28,Default,,0,0,0,,The front army is only\N thirty {\i1}li{\i0} away from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.28,0:08:10.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep scouting.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.50,0:08:11.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.00,0:08:19.28,Default,,0,0,0,,By orders of the King of Wei, I am here to take your head.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.28,0:08:21.73,Default,,0,0,0,,If you do not believe me, \Nyour coffin is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.73,0:08:25.08,Default,,0,0,0,,If you fear death, then submit right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.24,0:08:31.48,Default,,0,0,0,,What ability do you, a common brute, have?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.48,0:08:34.02,Default,,0,0,0,,What a pity that my \NGreen Dragon Crescent Blade
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.02,0:08:36.08,Default,,0,0,0,,has to cut down an\N unworthy rat like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.68,0:09:03.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Ring the bell.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.15,0:09:14.57,Default,,0,0,0,,General Yu, the King made you\N the main general over the seven armies.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.15,0:09:18.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you so timid\N on the battlefield, General?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.80,0:09:26.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, I will battle Guan Yu\N to the death. I vow not to retreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.15,0:09:35.00,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Pang De's skill with the glaive\N is refined and flawless.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.00,0:09:37.08,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,He counts as a worthy foe for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.55,0:09:39.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, I shall battle him again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.20,0:09:43.35,Default,,0,0,0,,If I do not cut him down, I will not back away.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.62,0:09:48.26,Default,,0,0,0,,As the idiom says, newborn calves are not afraid of tigers.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.26,0:09:50.68,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Even if father were to cut this man down,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.68,0:09:53.62,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,he is just a Western Qiang soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.69,0:09:54.14,Note (Potential style?),NTP,0,0,0,,Western Qiāng(西羌): Northern nomadic peoples who lived in Liang province, northwest China.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.86,0:09:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,If you make the slightest error, \Nmy uncle's trust would be let down.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.22,0:10:01.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Please think carefully before acting, father.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.91,0:10:06.17,Default,,0,0,0,,My mind has been set, say no more.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.65,0:10:14.22,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}I have gained no glory yet\N despite being the leading officer.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.22,0:10:17.54,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}How could I let this Western Qiang \Nsoldier get them before me?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.46,0:10:20.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not shoot that arrow, cursed Pang!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.02,0:10:23.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Ring the bell, ring the bell!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.75,0:10:37.53,Default,,0,0,0,,What is happening in the rear army?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.53,0:10:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The rear army is safe and sound.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.42,0:10:42.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Then why ring the bell to retreat?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.51,0:10:47.48,Default,,0,0,0,,General Pang, his Highness warned us \Nthat Guan Yu is both wise and brave.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.48,0:10:50.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if he was shot, \Nhe may have other wile tricks.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.18,0:10:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Ergo, the bell was rung.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.62,0:10:52.75,Default,,0,0,0,,You...!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.97,0:10:58.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Defend the gates.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.06,0:11:00.66,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter how much \NPang De curses, do not report.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.66,0:11:01.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.94,0:11:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I cannot be seen as being timid of battle \Nby that peasant due to an injury.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.06,0:11:07.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Ready my horse!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.82,0:11:09.53,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Please rest for a few days.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.53,0:11:12.18,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,There will be time \Nfor revenge after you recover.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.18,0:11:13.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed, General.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.86,0:11:19.56,Default,,0,0,0,,The way I see it, \NGuan Yu must be in fear of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.56,0:11:21.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Hence, he has refused\N to fight for this long.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.82,0:11:23.64,Default,,0,0,0,,We should exploit this situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.44,0:11:27.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us gather the seven armies \Nand overwhelm his camp,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.97,0:11:30.12,Default,,0,0,0,,thus breaking the siege at Fancheng.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.04,0:11:34.28,Default,,0,0,0,,General, please make a decision soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.86,0:11:41.27,Default,,0,0,0,,General Pang, we must not act rashly,\N as was clearly ordered by his Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.57,0:11:46.61,Default,,0,0,0,,How could we be disobedient?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.69,0:11:53.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Better to wait for a \Ngood plan to present itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.89,0:11:56.77,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Ever since we marched here,\N you have not made a single plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.77,0:11:58.76,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,How long will you delay for?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.22,0:12:08.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}I have marched with\N his Highness for thirty years,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.10,0:12:10.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}is that enough time to be a general?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.61,0:12:15.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord8\pos(640,672)}Though you know spirited bravery,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.08,0:12:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}you fail to know strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.81,0:12:27.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}I am going to pass this order:
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.78,0:12:30.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}because the weather is sweltering,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.84,0:12:33.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}I will lead the seven armies to camp next to a mountain opening
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.74,0:12:39.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}ten {\i1}li{\i0} north of Fancheng tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.02,0:12:46.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}You will take your command \Nand camp in the valley behind us.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.85,0:12:50.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}General, the army not only does not advance, but also retreats!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.74,0:12:52.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}This seems wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.77,0:12:58.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Ignore Guan Yu's moment of glory.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.52,0:13:05.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Looking ahead, there \Nis trouble for Jing Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.02,0:13:09.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}His Highness sent an envoy \Nto Sun Quan beforehand,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.66,0:13:12.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}asking Eastern Wu to attack Jing through naval routes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.61,0:13:14.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}When the Wu troops act,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.50,0:13:17.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Guan Yu will retreat \Nto defend Jing Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.42,0:13:20.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Then, I will gather the seven armies
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.22,0:13:23.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}and take advantage \Nof his retreat to strike!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.02,0:13:25.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}He will struggle to defend \Nboth his front and rear,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.34,0:13:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}will we not break him\N with a single strike?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.40,0:13:35.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}And will the siege at Fancheng not resolve itself?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.04,0:13:38.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}It as the {\i1}Art of War{\i0} advises:
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.90,0:13:42.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}"Stay still and gain the advantage."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.37,0:13:48.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Report!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.82,0:13:54.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Yu Jin moved all his seven armies to a valley opening ten {\i1}li{\i0} north of the city.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.13,0:13:55.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}His motive is unknown.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.89,0:14:00.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Then where is Pang De now?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.44,0:14:02.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Pang De is garrisoned in the valley.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.01,0:14:26.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Scout!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.36,0:14:29.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Here, General Guan.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.77,0:14:33.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Does that valley have a name to it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.10,0:14:35.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}It's name is Zengkou Valley.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.74,0:14:38.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Zengkou Valley?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.05,0:14:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Yes, Zengkou Valley.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.20,0:14:49.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu Jin will be captured by me for certain.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.07,0:14:51.66,Default,,0,0,0,,General, how do you know that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.04,0:14:55.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}A {\i1}zeng{\i0} is a net.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.27,0:14:58.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Once the "fish" enters the net, even it is not captured,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.08,0:14:59.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}surely it does not have a way out?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.04,0:14:56.76,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,A play on words. Fish (鱼) sounds similar to the surname Yu (于).
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.02,0:15:16.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Yu Jin's choosing not to garrison on open ground,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.40,0:15:24.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}but on a chokepoint such as Zengkou Valley, is a grave strategic mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.90,0:15:28.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Now, with the incessant autumn rain,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.77,0:15:33.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}the water level of the Xiang river will rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.26,0:15:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}I ordered Liao Hua and others to go to the upper reaches separately
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.00,0:15:40.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}to block the river at multiple points.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.49,0:15:42.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Once the water level rises,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.17,0:15:45.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}our army can mount boats \Nat high ground and release the water.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.50,0:15:47.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}The Cao soldiers at Fancheng and Zengkou valley...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.86,0:15:49.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}... Will be like fishes and turtles!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.74,0:16:02.84,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,... As the main general, \NI have led armies for decades,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.84,0:16:04.75,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,you mean to say I am lesser than you!?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.77,0:16:08.92,Default,,0,0,0,,But we are at the mouth \Nof a very low river valley.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.14,0:16:08.34,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,1820,2180)\pos(962,444)}Chéng Hé
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.92,0:16:11.89,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,If the river rises with \Nthe recent downpour,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.89,0:16:13.70,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,will our army not be in danger?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.32,0:16:17.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I will kill you if you dare \Nyell drivel and disturb morale again!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.70,0:16:18.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Leave!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.78,0:16:19.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.40,0:16:46.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu Jin, you cretin! \NYou deserve a miserable death!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.78,0:16:48.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu Jin!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.68,0:16:59.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You cretin! \NYou deserve a miserable death!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.12,0:17:01.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu Jin, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.14,0:18:48.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I wish to surrender! I wish to surrender!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.08,0:18:57.34,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Send him to prison in Jing Province under escort.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.34,0:18:59.27,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Once I return, he will be dealt with.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.27,0:18:59.90,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.50,0:19:00.54,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(336,470)}Liào Huà\NStyled: Yuánjiǎn
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.88,0:19:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Guan Yu is coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.40,0:19:24.26,Default,,0,0,0,,General Cheng, go and meet the enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.26,0:19:24.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.46,0:19:26.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.32,0:19:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Petulant Pang De, you are still defiant. \NWhat are you waiting for?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.96,0:19:35.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Guan Yu, you lout, come up to \Nthe embankment and fight to the death!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.76,0:19:36.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Loose!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.59,0:19:46.62,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,General Pang, we have\N too many casualties!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.62,0:19:50.65,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,With nowhere to go,\N why not surrender?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.60,0:19:54.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I have received favor from the King!\N How can I be servile to others?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.67,0:20:33.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}A brave general is not afraid to die,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.34,0:20:35.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}a fighter will not sully his morals to live!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.62,0:20:38.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}I hope you will continue \Nfighting by my side!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.72,0:20:41.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Please stay behind! Let me charge first!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.70,0:21:15.50,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,1500,1780)\pos(290.667,434.667)}Zhōu Cāng
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.85,0:21:49.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Bring Pang De here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.36,0:21:55.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Kneel!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.72,0:21:58.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Kneel!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.06,0:22:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Pang De, your elder brother is serving \Nthe King of Hanzhong as an official.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.41,0:22:14.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Ma Chao, your past lord, is also serving the King of Hanzhong as a general.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.97,0:22:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not surrender right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.13,0:22:21.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I would rather die under the sword!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.10,0:22:22.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Why surrender?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.00,0:22:24.78,Default,,0,0,0,,You are a disgrace!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.61,0:22:29.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Execute him.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.18,0:22:33.94,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,1300,1740)\pos(330.667,464)}Cáo Rén\NStyled: Zǐxiào
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.38,0:22:38.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Ren, you fool!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.06,0:22:41.14,Default,,0,0,0,,If Pang De and Yu Jin\N were not worthy foes to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.14,0:22:43.40,Default,,0,0,0,,then how can you insects be as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.40,0:22:46.60,Default,,0,0,0,,You have not surrendered yet! \NWhat are you waiting for?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.07,0:22:49.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Shoot the poison arrows!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.27,0:22:50.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Loose!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.18,0:22:54.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.68,0:22:55.38,Default,,0,0,0,,General Guan!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.78,0:23:06.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.94,0:23:09.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Young General, where is his Lordship?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.38,0:23:12.46,Default,,0,0,0,,He is waiting for you, sir, in the tent.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.46,0:23:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, let us go there now.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.18,0:23:14.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.20,0:23:18.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.10,0:23:20.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,2450,2740)\pos(322,466.667)}Huà Tuó\NStyled: Yuánhuà
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.46,0:23:20.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.70,0:23:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.66,0:23:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.32,0:23:28.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Good, good.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.62,0:23:31.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I am affected by a minor ailment.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.58,0:23:34.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, how did you know of it\N all the way from Jiangdong?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.26,0:23:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,The wound is on your right arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.25,0:23:44.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Please undress.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.96,0:23:48.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, you endured an arduous trip.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.06,0:23:51.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Please rest now, as it is not too late to treat this later.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.74,0:23:55.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Your health is important, how can I delay?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.86,0:23:57.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Please undress now.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.12,0:24:41.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}This wound was \Ncaused by a crossbow.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:41.50,0:24:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Once the bolt is poisoned, it can penetrate flesh and bone.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:46.77,0:24:50.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Luckily, if this wound went untreated\N for two or three more days,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.62,0:24:54.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}your arm might have \Nbeen too late to save.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.27,0:24:58.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}If I follow your meaning, do you know of an existing treatment?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.58,0:25:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}My presence is the beginning of the cure.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.56,0:25:07.05,Default,,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.66,0:25:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.42,0:25:16.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}I view death as a homecoming. \NWhat is there to fear?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.32,0:25:18.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}What will the method of treatment be?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.26,0:25:19.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Feel free to say it!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:23.58,0:25:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}First, I will raise a pillar in a quiet area, nailing a large ring onto it.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.69,0:25:32.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Then, you would extend \Nthe wounded arm into the ring,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.80,0:25:34.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}with rope being used to secure it.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.56,0:25:37.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Next, I will get a thick blanket to cover your head and face.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.80,0:25:40.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Afterwards, the poison can be treated.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:41.06,0:25:43.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Sir, if it is my right arm\N that is to be treated,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:44.76,0:25:46.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}why cover my head and face?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.37,0:25:51.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Any treatment of the bone \Nmust be done this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.45,0:25:56.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}During the treatment, \Nthe skin and the flesh flare out
Dialogue: 0,0:25:56.24,0:25:58.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}and blood gushes out.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:58.18,0:26:02.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}The patient will of course be horrified by the sight.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:02.82,0:26:06.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}With him trembling in fear, it's difficult to proceed.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.08,0:26:14.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Sir, do you not use \Na knife during such a treatment?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.04,0:26:19.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}First, I use a sharp knife to cut the skin and flesh all the way to the bone.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:19.77,0:26:23.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Then, I scrape away the poison from the bone {\bord11}and treat the opening with medicine.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:23.48,0:26:27.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Finally, I use thin strings \Nto stitch the wound,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:27.26,0:26:29.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}and all will be settled.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:34.57,0:26:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}What does your knife look like, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:57.94,0:27:01.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}This knife is a hundred times smaller than my Green Dragon Blade,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:01.29,0:27:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}but sharper than it!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:05.52,0:27:07.18,Default,,0,0,0,,You overpraise it, General.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.18,0:27:08.56,Default,,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:27:10.73,0:27:12.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You are worried that I am afraid?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.56,0:27:21.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Cutting the skin and flesh\N all the way to the bone,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.98,0:27:23.57,Default,,0,0,0,,way easier than I thought!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.57,0:27:24.69,Default,,0,0,0,,-My son Guan Ping!\N-Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:24.69,0:27:25.88,Default,,0,0,0,,-Prepare the wine.\N-Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:25.88,0:27:26.66,Default,,0,0,0,,-Jichang!\N-Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:26.66,0:27:27.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us play.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:37.26,0:27:38.90,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,1300,1620)\pos(316,458.667)}Mǎ Liáng\NStyled: Jìcháng
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.37,0:27:53.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Master Hua Tuo,\N why are you not starting?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.17,0:27:58.70,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I am waiting for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:58.70,0:28:02.44,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Have the pillar and the ring \Nbeen prepared yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.40,0:28:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,They are unnecessary \Nwhen you cut into my flesh.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:09.41,0:28:13.85,Default,,0,0,0,,General, the pain will be unbearable!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:15.30,0:28:19.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I am no ordinary man,\N how can I fear pain?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.88,0:28:23.13,Default,,0,0,0,,But you also have a \Nbody of flesh and blood!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.13,0:28:27.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I have heard that you treated blade \Nwounds for Zhou Tai of Eastern Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.12,0:28:30.14,Default,,0,0,0,,How was his injury compared to mine?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.80,0:28:33.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Similar.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.34,0:28:37.28,Default,,0,0,0,,General Zhou of Wu \Nhad tens of blade wounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:37.28,0:28:39.50,Default,,0,0,0,,His appearance was grisly!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:40.14,0:28:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,,However, the wounds had no poison,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:43.02,0:28:46.53,Default,,0,0,0,,so I only needed to dress them \Nand they would heal.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.53,0:28:51.40,Default,,0,0,0,,He did not suffer the pain of cut flesh and scraped bone!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.77,0:28:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Master Hua Tuo, I have \Nspent my entire life as a soldier
Dialogue: 0,0:28:56.46,0:28:58.30,Default,,0,0,0,,and view death as a homecoming.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:58.30,0:29:01.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would I fear \Nthe pain of scraped bone?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:02.56,0:29:06.40,Default,,0,0,0,,What more needs to be said \Nwhen you are saving my arm?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:06.40,0:29:07.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I can bear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:07.95,0:29:12.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Before the wine wears off, \Nplease be brave and take action!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.90,0:31:00.34,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,2000,2420)\pos(856,370.667)}Wáng Fǔ
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.36,0:31:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,General, the treatment is complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:37.02,0:31:38.53,Default,,0,0,0,,This quickly?!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.53,0:31:39.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Excellency!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:39.66,0:31:41.90,Default,,0,0,0,,-Father, Father!\N-General!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:50.35,0:31:53.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Master Hua Tuo, Master Hua Tuo!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.98,0:31:57.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:07.60,0:32:13.23,Default,,0,0,0,,General, I have practiced \Nmedicine my entire life.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:14.24,0:32:18.08,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I have treated no fewer\N than thousands of patients,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:18.08,0:32:21.98,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,but I have never seen \Nsomeone like you General.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:27.82,0:32:31.28,Default,,0,0,0,,General, you are truly extraordinary!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.48,0:32:36.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, my entire life \Nhas been spent as a soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:36.34,0:32:39.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I can simply handle some pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:39.58,0:32:42.97,Default,,0,0,0,,How can I compare to your techniques that bring the dead back to life?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:42.97,0:32:44.44,Default,,0,0,0,,You are admirable!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.50,0:32:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,They are but trivial skills,\N unworthy of being mentioned.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:49.00,0:32:53.30,Default,,0,0,0,,General, your mettle \Nis unparalleled in the world!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.25,0:33:01.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Having met you, General, \Nand being able to treat your wound,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.86,0:33:05.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I now know that I have not practiced medicine my entire life in vain!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.14,0:33:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, you overpraise me.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:17.04,0:33:18.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Astonishing!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.48,0:33:25.84,Default,,0,0,0,,This arm can be extended \Nat will without any pain!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.42,0:33:31.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You, sir, truly are a miracle healer!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:31.65,0:33:32.98,Default,,0,0,0,,You flatter me!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:33.46,0:33:39.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Although the arrow poison is gone,\N one hundred days of rest is still needed.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.60,0:33:43.22,Default,,0,0,0,,A full recovery is possible \Nif you keep calm.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.24,0:33:47.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I am giving you this medicine.\N Please apply it on your wound.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.56,0:33:52.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.98,0:34:03.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I know that you are not interested in money,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:03.17,0:34:09.90,Default,,0,0,0,,but I prepared some funds for \Nyour travel to express my gratitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:09.90,0:34:16.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no ulterior motives.\N I hope that you will accept this, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:16.25,0:34:17.48,Default,,0,0,0,,What is the meaning of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:18.00,0:34:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:19.63,0:34:23.98,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I heard that you are one of the \Nworld's heroes and a stalwart warrior.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.98,0:34:27.64,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Therefore, I came from afar \Nto treat your wound.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:27.64,0:34:30.50,Default,,0,0,0,,How could I want any sort of reward?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:30.95,0:34:34.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Knowing you is enough satisfaction.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:34.12,0:34:35.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I will not take this.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:36.44,0:34:38.74,Default,,0,0,0,,General, take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:38.74,0:34:41.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Farewell, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:43.81,0:34:45.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.49,0:35:02.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, your phenomenal methods \Nalways aids the common folk.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:03.41,0:35:06.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, please take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:39.31,0:35:42.30,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Guan Yu has laid beacons\N along the Yangzi river
Dialogue: 0,0:35:42.30,0:35:47.02,Thinking,,0,0,0,,to watch out for our \Nadvance on Jing Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:49.86,0:35:52.65,Thinking,,0,0,0,,What can be done?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.54,0:35:54.54,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,1620,1980)\pos(309.333,469.333)}Lǚ Méng\NStyled: Zǐmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:36:00.90,0:36:03.66,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,360,2390,2740)\pos(304,464)}Lù Xùn\NStyled: Bóyán
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.04,0:36:38.60,Default,,0,0,0,,The Marquis of Wu\N has given you a major task.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:38.60,0:36:40.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You have not done anything, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.33,0:36:43.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You could have executed a pincer attack to seize Jing.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:43.57,0:36:47.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Instead, you are freely sitting \Nhere and sighing. Why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:55.84,0:36:59.52,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I have a small cure for your illness.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:59.52,0:37:02.16,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,What are your thoughts on it?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:02.76,0:37:05.66,Default,,0,0,0,,What good cure do you have,\N Boyan? Please tell me now.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:06.53,0:37:10.22,Default,,0,0,0,,In my opinion, your body has no illness.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:10.22,0:37:11.70,Default,,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:37:15.85,0:37:20.91,Default,,0,0,0,,you wanted to attack and take Jing \Nper the orders of the Marquis of Wu,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:20.91,0:37:23.04,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,unaware that the cities are well-guarded,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:23.04,0:37:26.61,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,and also impenetrable with the\N beacons along the Yangzi river.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:26.61,0:37:29.98,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,General, you fear you cannot \Nreport back to the Marquis of Wu,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:29.98,0:37:33.56,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,hence you feign illness to stay here.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:36.69,0:37:40.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a stratagem that can render the beacons unable to light fires,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:40.53,0:37:43.85,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,causing the soldiers of Jing to surrender.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:43.85,0:37:47.73,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Might it heal your illness?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:48.34,0:37:51.06,Default,,0,0,0,,You speak as if you \Nknow what I am thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:51.06,0:37:52.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I would like to hear the stratagem.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:54.55,0:37:58.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}General, Guan Yu sees himself as peerless in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:58.67,0:38:01.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}He sees us Wu generals as inferior.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:01.17,0:38:04.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}The only man who\N he worries about is you, General.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:04.37,0:38:07.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}General, do seize this moment to resign due to "illness"
Dialogue: 0,0:38:07.13,0:38:10.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}so you can transfer the duties of Lukou to another man.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:10.25,0:38:15.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Do also find a way to please \NGuan Yu, making him arrogant.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:15.36,0:38:18.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Thus, he will move the troops in Jing to his attack on Fancheng.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.53,0:38:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}With Jing Province empty and defenseless,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:21.21,0:38:23.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}our army can attack it in surprise.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:23.88,0:38:27.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}How will this not achieve\N victory after only one battle?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:28.78,0:38:32.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What a brilliant stratagem! I will \Nsubmit my resignation this instant.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:36.80,0:38:38.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Were it not for the arrow wound,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:38.70,0:38:42.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I would have already taken Fancheng and moved the army further north.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:42.48,0:38:45.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Cao has sent Xu Huang\Nto reinforce Fancheng.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:45.08,0:38:48.72,Default,,0,0,0,,If we stall any further, will we not lose a great opportunity?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:48.72,0:38:51.93,Default,,0,0,0,,The troops might be too few for an immediate assault.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:51.93,0:38:54.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, Lu Xun, Eastern Wu's defending general at Lukou,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:54.75,0:38:57.62,Default,,0,0,0,,has sent an emissary \Nwith gifts to visit to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:59.50,0:39:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Lu Xun?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:08.14,0:39:12.93,Default,,0,0,0,,General Guan, due to \NGeneral Lü Meng being severely ill,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:16.60,0:39:16.94,Default,,0,0,0,,he has been assigned back to Jianye by the Marquis of Wu to recuperate.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:16.94,0:39:21.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Lukou is now overseen by General Lu Xun, who is the replacement.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:21.45,0:39:26.22,Default,,0,0,0,,General Lu sent me to bring paltry gifts to send his regards to you, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:27.01,0:39:30.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I only know that Lu Xun \Nis the son-in-law of Sun Ce.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:30.89,0:39:36.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I have not heard about any \Naccomplishments of his in the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:37.54,0:39:41.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Sun Quan is shortsighted to use such a child as a general.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.98,0:39:47.37,Default,,0,0,0,,General Lu has a letter for your Lordship.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:47.37,0:39:49.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Firstly, it expresses\N his congratulations to you,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:49.94,0:39:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,and secondly, it asks\N for peace between our two realms.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:00.70,0:40:04.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}I, Lu Xun, respectfully present\N this letter to the Marquis of Hanshou,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.30,0:40:07.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Yunchang, one of \Nthe Five Tiger Generals!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.44,0:40:09.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}I heard that you led\N an army to attack the traitor,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:09.88,0:40:12.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}winning huge with little action. \NYou captured Yu Jin
Dialogue: 0,0:40:12.56,0:40:15.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}and decapitated Pang De. \NThose far and wide have rejoiced!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:15.60,0:40:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Sir, your accomplishments are truly...
Dialogue: 0,0:40:19.60,0:40:24.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Although Lu Xun has no military merits, \Nhe is self-aware of that fact.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:24.23,0:40:28.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I accept these gifts. Go tell \NGeneral Lu that I am thankful.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:30.13,0:40:31.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:38.36,0:40:44.46,Default,,0,0,0,,If this is the case, then the \Nthreat from Jiangdong is no more!

